   "type": "text",
   "text": "```yaml\n- id: DR-01\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a dispatcher see which of their drones could reach where a job starts, and it must not choose a drone or a route for the dispatcher.\n- id: DR-02\n  requirement: >\n    The service must leave the decision of which drone flies and along which route to the dispatcher.\n- id: DR-03\n  requirement: >\n    The service must support several dispatchers planning flights at the same time for the same busy sites and popular drones.\n- id: DR-04\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not send a drone on a flight until a licensed dispatcher has signed off that flight.\n- id: DR-05\n  requirement: >\n    The service must record which dispatcher signed off each flight.\n- id: DR-06\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a dispatcher call off a flight, including a flight already signed off, before it leaves.\n- id: DR-07\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not be restarted or updated during working hours, except for an interruption of a few minutes.\n- id: DR-08\n  requirement: >\n    The service must handle an instruction sent to a drone or charging equipment that arrives more than once without causing a second, unintended action.\n- id: DR-09\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let the sender of an instruction to a drone or charging equipment find out whether that instruction arrived.\n- id: DR-10\n  requirement: >\n    The service must accept drone reports that arrive late, out of order, more than once, or not at all, and must not treat any of these as a valid current state without checking.\n- id: DR-11\n  requirement: >\n    The service must hold a shared picture of the flight corridor network between sites, the zones that group those sites, and the closures announced by authorities.\n- id: DR-12\n  requirement: >\n    The service must record each planned closure with its start and end times, and must apply each sudden closure as soon as it is entered.\n- id: DR-13\n  requirement: >\n    The service must accept amendments to a closure made during the day and must apply each amendment to the shared picture.\n- id: DR-14\n  requirement: >\n    When a closure is entered or amended, the service must show the airspace desk how much disruption it causes across customers.\n- id: DR-15\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a fleet technician add a drone to the fleet, retire a drone, take a drone out of service for repair, return it to service, and send a drone to charge.\n- id: DR-16\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a fleet technician set up charging pads at sites.\n- id: DR-17\n  requirement: >\n    The service must keep a maintenance history for each drone and be able to produce it on request for a regulator.\n- id: DR-18\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not be treated as complete for fleet technicians or the airspace desk until their needs have been gathered, because their interviews produced no usable detail beyond the duties and records stated above.\n```"
